// Package pycompat holds the Python 3.15 behaviour the ported tools must reproduce byte for
// byte: repr()/str() of values, float repr and "%g", int()/float() parsing, %-formatting
// with a mapping, the str predicates (isalpha, isdecimal, isdigit, isnumeric, isalnum,
// isprintable, isspace, re's \w) from tables generated by the Python itself, strip/split/
// splitlines, bytes.decode("utf-8", "replace"), html.escape (html.unescape forwards to pyhtml), os.path.join (Join, over pypath),
// str.isupper() and str.lower(), ljust/rjust and s[:n] by code points, and format(value, spec) (the format-spec
// mini-language of str.format and f-strings) for str, int and float with Commas for format(n, ","), str(OSError) and
// os.strerror for Go os errors (Linux and Windows tables), text-file universal newlines, cp437 decoding
// of zip member names, zipfile's last-entry-wins member lookup, base64.b64decode's lenient decoding,
// os.listdir and sorted(os.listdir) (Listdir, SortedListdir), sorted(set(xs)) (SortedSet), and
// os.walk (Walk, WalkWith: top-down, sorted or os.scandir order, optional onerror),
// os.makedirs with its FileExistsError and NotADirectoryError paths (Makedirs), and
// hashlib.sha256 of a file's bytes (FileSHA256).
//
// unicode.txt, errno_linux.txt, testdata/fixtures.json and the testdata/golden/format_*.golden
// cases are frozen output of the retired testdata/gen.py, and errno_windows.txt of the retired
// testdata/gen_windows.py (a Windows Python); they change only from reviewed Go output. The
// tests replay every fixture and golden and hash every code point against Python's digests.
package pycompat
